      "Australia's Digital Trade Strategy states that digital trade and digital technologies 'have the potential to level the playing field and promote inclusive growth by unlocking opportunities, new technologies and markets to MSMEs, women-run businesses and others...'. The Strategy also refers to Australia's aid for trade investment initiatives promoting the use of digital technologies to make trade more inclusive, supporting the uptake of e-commerce to make trade cheaper, more efficient and more accessible to disadvantaged groups, including women.  "
