      "Australia supports women's participation in the digital economy and trade through broader skills, workforce participation, entrepreneurship and STEM initiatives rather than through dedicated programs specifically targeting women in digital trade. These measures help build the skills, capabilities and opportunities needed for women to participate in digitally enabled sectors and economic activities.\n\nThrough its international development and Aid for Trade program, Australia also supports women's participation in digital trade and the digital economy in partner countries. This includes support for women's digital financial inclusion, e-commerce readiness, digital capability and women-led businesses through initiatives such as the UNCTAD E-Commerce and Digital Economy Programme and regional trade and gender initiatives. (see response on eTrade for Women, TFSP, TSCFP, RT4D & PIFS at Q5)."
