     "main": "Australia's strategic direction operates through complementary domestic and international policy streams. Domestically, broader gender equality, skills, STEM, workforce participation, entrepreneurship and digital capability programs look to address structural barriers and strengthen women's pathways into digitally enabled sectors, rather than operating as dedicated digital trade programs. \n\nInternationally, Australia uses trade policy and development assistance support more direct participation by women in digital trade in partner countries. This includes initiatives such as Regional Trade for Development (RT4D), which delivers targeted training, mentoring, business networks and capacity building on e-commerce, digital entrepreneurship and cross-border trade for women and women-led MSMEs in ASEAN. Together, these streams apply a common strategic objective-addressing constraints in skills, finance, market access and economic participation-through instruments suited to Australia's domestic context and the needs and priorities of partner countries.\n\nLinks:\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/trade/services-and-digital-trade/e-commerce-and-digital-trade/digital-trade-strategy\n\nhttps://www.pmc.gov.au/office-women/working-women-strategy-gender-equality\n\nhttps://www.homeaffairs.gov.au/about-us/our-portfolios/cyber-security/strategy/2023-2030-australian-cyber-security-strategy\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/countries-economies-and-regions/southeast-asia/invested-australias-southeast-asia-economic-strategy-2040/chapter-10-digital-economy\n\nhttps://www.industry.gov.au/publications/statement-pathway-diversity-stem-review\n\nhttps://www.dewr.gov.au/building-womens-careers-program\n\nhttps://www.dewr.gov.au/national-skills-agreement\n\nhttps://unctad.org/topic/ecommerce-and-digital-economy\n\nhttps://forumsec.org/pacific-e-commerce-initiative\n\nhttps://pacificecommerce.org/reports/pacific-regional-e-commerce-strategy-and-roadmap/\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/publications/development/australias-international-gender-equality-strategy\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/publications/development/australias-international-development-policy\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/trade/agreements/in-force/aukfta/official-text/australia-uk-fta-chapter-14-digital-trade\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/trade/agreements/in-force/australia-uae-comprehensive-economic-partnership-agreement-cepa/australia-uae-cepa-official-text/chapter-12-digital-trade\n\nhttps://www.dfat.gov.au/sites/default/files/second-protocol-to-amend-the-agreement-establishing-the-asean-australia-new-zealand.pdf\n\nhttps://www.austrade.gov.au/en/how-we-can-help-you/programs-and-services/landing-pads\n\nhttps://export.business.gov.au/\n\nhttps://www.apec.org/meeting-papers/sectoral-ministerial-meetings/trade/2023-apec-ministers-responsible-for-trade-statement-of-the-chair/annex-1\n\nhttps://ftaportal.dfat.gov.au/\n\nhttps://www.dewr.gov.au/skills-reform/free-tafe\n\nhttps://www.industry.gov.au/publications/stem-equity-monitor\n\nhttps://unctad.org/topic/ecommerce-and-digital-economy/etrade-for-women\n\nhttps://unctad.org/meeting/etrade-women-masterclass-south-east-asia-and-pacific\n\nhttps://business.gov.au/grants-and-programs/women-in-stem-and-entrepreneurship\n\nhttps://sciencegenderequity.org.au/\n\nhttps://www.austrade.gov.au/en/how-we-can-help-you/programs-and-services/simplified-trade-system\n\nhttps://www.atse.org.au/what-we-do/pathways-into-through-stem/elevate/\n\n\n\n",
