      "Bulgaria ranks high in the EU in terms of share of women in the ICT sector (about 25% according to Eurostat data - https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/isoc_sks_itsps/default/table?lang=en). Women are equally included in all policies, programs and projects in the field of digital economy, digital transformation, e-commerce, or digital trade. All projects under the EU funded programmes observe the equality principle and stimulates women inclusion. \n\nThe Digital Transformation Strategy of the Republic of Bulgaria 2024-2030 (https://www.strategy.bg/bg/strategy-documents/1687 ) is a key strategic document developed by the former Ministry of e-Government, currently the Ministry of Innovation and Digital Transformation, which includes a specific focus on women, indicating them as a key target group in several areas. \nOther main strategic frameworks that address measures aimed at women or encouraging women entrepreneurship:\n1. National Program \"Digital Bulgaria 2025\" - https://www.strategy.bg/bg/strategy-documents/1315 \n2. National Recovery and Resilience Plan (NRRP) - https://www.strategy.bg/bg/strategy-documents/1522 \n3. National Strategy for Promoting Gender Equality: http://strategy.bg/bg/strategy-documents/1362 \n4. National Strategy for SMEs 2021-2027 (extended to 2030): https://www.strategy.bg/bg/strategy-documents/1730.\n"
