      "The initiatives and programmes linked to Chile's MSME digitalisation and entrepreneurship ecosystem cover a broad set of intervention areas. \"Digitaliza tu Pyme\" focuses on digital maturity diagnosis, digital and entrepreneurial skills, e-commerce training, technical assistance, access to digital technologies, digital payments, cybersecurity awareness and data-based segmentation. Through \"Chequeo Digital\", firms can assess their level of digital maturity and be guided toward more relevant support pathways according to their needs, sector, territory and stage of digital adoption.\nThe programme also connects MSMEs with training and support services related to online sales, customer management, digital marketing, digital tools for business management and access to digital markets. Some initiatives, such as \"Digitaliza tu Almacén\", support small retail businesses in adopting practical technologies such as point-of-sale systems, electronic invoicing, inventory management tools and digital payment solutions.\nExport readiness is covered more selectively. The \"Digitaliza tu Pyme\" team supports initiatives such as \"Fortalecimiento de Capacidades Exportadoras para MiPymes de la Alianza del Pacífico\", which seeks to strengthen MSMEs' capacity to participate in cross-border e-commerce.\nIn addition, Chile's broader public support ecosystem includes Corfo instruments with a specific focus on women-led businesses and startups. For example, \"Semilla Inicia\" para Empresas Lideradas por Mujeres supports innovative ventures led by women through co-financing, technical and commercial validation, mentoring and entrepreneurial skills development. Corfo has also opened \"Inicia\" and \"Expande\" calls for women-led innovative ventures, supporting firms from early validation stages to expansion into new markets.\nStart-Up Chile, Corfo's public startup accelerator, also includes gender-focused measures through \"Female Founder Factor\". This initiative seeks to empower women in the entrepreneurial ecosystem and is connected to programmes such as \"Build\", \"Ignite\" and \"Growth\", which include gender parity objectives or preferential funding conditions for startups with women leaders.\nTherefore, the covered areas include digital trade training, entrepreneurial skills, access to finance, digital payments, access to technologies, innovation and entrepreneurship support, mentoring, business networks, investment readiness for startups, and digital maturity diagnosis and data-based segmentation."
