      "Chile uses a combination of instruments to support women's participation in digital trade, mainly through general MSME digitalisation programmes that include women, and complementary women-focused export and entrepreneurship instruments.\nThe first group of instruments includes digital maturity diagnosis and data-based segmentation. \"Digitaliza tu Pyme\" uses \"Chequeo Digital\" to assess firms' digital maturity and guide them toward training, technical assistance and technology adoption pathways according to their needs, sector, territory and stage of development.\nA second group includes training and mentoring. Through \"Digitaliza tu Pyme\", \"Pymes en Línea\", \"Ruta Digital\", Sercotec Business Centres and Corfo's support networks, MSMEs can access training related to digital tools, online sales, digital marketing, business management, cybersecurity and e-commerce. These instruments are not exclusively for women, but women entrepreneurs participate as part of the MSME target population.\nChile also uses grants and subsidies for technology adoption. For example, \"Digitaliza tu Almacén\" supports small retail businesses through financial support and technical assistance for the adoption of point-of-sale systems, electronic invoicing, inventory management tools, financial control software and digital payment solutions.\nExport promotion services are provided through ProChile, including \"Mujer Exporta\", which supports women-led companies that are exporters or mature enough to export through training, networks, empowerment activities and commercial promotion. In addition, the \"Digitaliza tu Pyme\" team supports the Pacific Alliance initiative on strengthening MSME export capacities through cross-border e-commerce.\nDigital platform access is supported through public training platforms and, more broadly, through initiatives that connect firms to online tools, digital markets and business support services. Chile is also developing new platform-based approaches, such as initiatives to connect supply and demand from women-led companies.\nFinally, incubators and accelerators are part of the broader innovation ecosystem. Corfo has instruments for women-led innovative ventures, and Start-Up Chile includes gender-focused measures through \"Female Founder Factor\" and its \"Build\", \"Ignite\" and \"Growth\" programmes.\nOverall, the instruments combine diagnosis, training, mentoring, grants, technology adoption, digital payments, export promotion, platform access and startup acceleration."
