      "National Plan for the Promotion of Exports of the Dominican Republic 2020-2030\nPillar 1/ Measures\n1.1.1.3. Develop a strategy to increase women's participation in the chain of prioritized export goods and services, favoring equity and women's empowerment.\n1.1.1.4. Support for entrepreneurial initiatives for the export of goods and services, supported by training, mentoring, technical assistance, linkage and financing programs through the planning of the resources available for the promotion of exports, such as e-commerce, digital marketing and appropriate delivery logistics.\nNational Development Strategy of the Dominican Republic 2030 (Law 1-12)\nArticle 12. Gender Approach. In accordance with this law, all plans, programs, projects and public policies must incorporate the gender approach in their respective areas of action.\nLines of action:\n3.4.2.5 Develop training programs that encourage the insertion of women in non-traditional sectors, and take into account the balance of productive and reproductive work.\n3.4.2.7 Promote the use of information and communication technologies as a tool to expand the scope of vocational and technical training."
