      "The following certificates are provided in the SheTrades-ecomConnect program:\n•Adoption of international certifications in agro-exports\n•Basics of International Trade\n•Business Intelligence\n•Internationalization of SMEs\n•Generating confidence in export\n•Certification as an access tool\n\nReference:\n•https://prodominicana.gob.do/shetrades#trainings\n\nMICM's training and business support initiatives focus on developing the practical capabilities entrepreneurs need to compete in an increasingly digital and globally connected economy. The Ministry adopts an integrated approach that combines digital competencies with entrepreneurship, innovation, business management and export-oriented skills, enabling women-owned enterprises to adopt digital business models, improve competitiveness and access new markets.\n\n\nThrough workshops, technical assistance, mentoring and collaboration with national and international partners, MICM strengthens capacities in areas such as digital business management, e-commerce, digital marketing, export readiness, market analysis and the adoption of emerging technologies. These efforts help entrepreneurs improve their operations, make informed business decisions, adapt to technological changes and participate more effectively in domestic and international digital markets."
