     "notes": [
      "Ecuador promotes women's participation in the digital economy and digital trade through a cross-cutting approach embedded within national policies on digital transformation, productive development, economic inclusion, and equal opportunities. Although not all strategic instruments contain women-specific measures for digital trade, they incorporate principles of inclusion, equitable access to digital technologies, and the reduction of structural digital divides affecting women entrepreneurs, producers, artisans, workers, and women-owned micro, small and medium-sized enterprises (MSMEs).\n\nIn this context, Ecuador's Digital Transformation Public Policy promotes the adoption of digital technologies to enhance productivity, competitiveness, innovation, and access to digital services while incorporating an inclusive approach aimed at reducing digital access and usage gaps across the population.\n\nComplementarily, the National Agenda for Gender Equality 2025-2029 establishes policy guidelines to strengthen women's economic empowerment by promoting equal participation in economic development, expanding access to productive opportunities, strengthening capacities, and addressing structural inequalities.\n\nEcuador is also developing the National Digital Trade Strategy 2030, which seeks to strengthen the national digital trade ecosystem through technological modernization, MSME digitalization, e-commerce development, trade facilitation, and enhanced coordination among public institutions, the private sector, academia, and international partners. Although the strategy has a broad national scope, it provides an important opportunity to further mainstream gender considerations into future implementation measures.\n\nIn parallel, Ecuador is implementing national programmes that indirectly contribute to women's participation in the digital economy, including EmpoderaTech Ecuador and its flagship initiatives such as Digitalízate Rural (Digitalize Rural), Empoderadas (Empowered Women), and the Productive Digital Transformation Roadmap. Additional initiatives include the nationwide Free Digital Points Network, together with digital skills and digital transformation programmes led by the Ministry of Telecommunications and the Information Society.\n\nAs well as tourism initiatives under development by the Ministry of Production, Foreign Trade and Investments, such as the \"Violet Tourism\" initiative, incorporates digital transformation with a gender perspective as one of its key areas of work, although it does not currently constitute a national strategy for the digital economy, digital transformation, e-commerce, or digital trade. Its contribution focuses on creating conditions that enable women involved in entrepreneurial ventures, community organizations, and tourism initiatives to strengthen their capabilities, leadership, and innovation, as well as gain progressive access to economic opportunities within the tourism value chain.\n"
     ]
