      "The skills covered correspond to the content of the E-Commerce and Social Media and Digital Platforms modules of \"Ella Exporta\" and to the training and technical assistance delivered by the E-Commerce Programme: e-commerce operations, understood as the process of entering, positioning and consolidating products on global digital platforms; digital marketing, through the use of social media and digital platforms for commercial positioning, complemented by branding content; and digital business management, as part of the business management and export management components of the programme.\nRegarding delivery formats, \"Ella Exporta\" combines two components: training, and technical assistance. Regarding the E-Commerce Programme, likewise combines training with company-level assistance throughout the process of digital market entry.\nUnder the ENME, the \"Thursdays for Women Entrepreneurs\" initiative is progressively incorporating skills related to business digitalization, based on the needs of women entrepreneurs and in coordination with specialized institutions.\nKey areas covered include digital literacy and the use of digital tools, business management, digital marketing, e-commerce, and the use of digital channels to promote and sell products. \nSpecialized content is also incorporated through coordination with public-sector institutions. For example, Ministry of Production (PRODUCE) provides digital training sessions covering digital marketing, social media management, e-commerce, artificial intelligence, and customer service in virtual environments. These activities complement the training opportunities available to women under the ENME.\nTraining is delivered mainly through in-person sessions, practical workshops, and virtual sessions, depending on the activity and location. In this regard, the \"Thursdays for Women Entrepreneurs\" initiative has combined in-person and virtual formats, helping expand access to business management content and tools across different regions.\n"
