      "PROMPERÚ's E-Commerce Programme can be understood as a technology adoption scheme for exporting SMEs: it supports companies in adopting digital sales channels and global e-commerce platforms as a route to international markets. The programme is open to all eligible SMEs in the food, apparel, jewelry, gift items and home decoration sectors, with no gender-specific track or quota. Nevertheless, historical participation records show that women entrepreneurs account for 57% of total participants.\nInclusion is reinforced through the \"Ella Exporta\" Programme for Leading Women Entrepreneurs, whose E-Commerce module informs participants of the existence of this instrument and encourages them to take it up, functioning in practice as a referral channel for women into PROMPERÚ's digital trade offer.\nUnder the National Strategy for Women Entrepreneurs (ENME), the Ministry of Women and Vulnerable Populations (MIMP) promotes women entrepreneurs' participation in capacity-building, innovation, and technology adoption initiatives through coordination with specialized public institutions. This coordination helps connect women entrepreneurs with opportunities related to innovation and technological transformation.\nThis approach reflects the fact that incubation, acceleration, and technology startup development programmes are mainly managed by specialized organizations within the business and innovation ecosystem. Therefore, in this area, the MIMP's role is to facilitate women entrepreneurs' access to these opportunities rather than to directly manage such programmes.\n"
