     "main": "The National Strategy for Action in the Interests of Women for 2023-2030 (hereinafter referred to as the Strategy) is a foundational document that defines the main directions of government policy in the interests of women. The Strategy seeks to consolidate the efforts of federal government agencies, government agencies of the constituent entities of the Russian Federation, local government bodies, the business community, nonprofit organizations, and citizens of the Russian Federation to promote the principle of equal rights and freedoms for men and women and to create equal opportunities for their realization.\nImprovements in the status of women over the past 5 years have been facilitated by measures implemented under strategic and policy documents, national projects, and government programs in the areas of the economy, education, employment, health care, and public welfare-such as the Concept of Demographic Policy of the Russian Federation for the Period up to 2025, approved by Decree of the President of the Russian Federation No. 1351 of October 9, 2007, the Concept of State Family Policy in the Russian Federation for the Period up to 2025, approved by Government Decree No. 1618-r of August 25, 2014, The Strategy for Action in the Interests of Senior Citizens in the Russian Federation through 2025, approved by Order of the Government of the Russian Federation No. 164-r of February 5, 2016, The National Strategy for Action in the Interests of Women for 2017-2022, approved by Decree of the Government of the Russian Federation No. 410-r of March 8, 2017, as well as the national projects \"Health Care,\" \"Education,\" \"Demographics, and \"Small and Medium-Sized Enterprises and Support for Individual Entrepreneurial Initiative.\"",
