     "main": "",
     "notes": [
      "The UK Government holds regular cross-Government Working Group meetings on Gender Equality to share information and facilitate coordination on ongoing activities.\nThe Department for Business, Innovation, Science and Trade (BIST) also runs regular Policy Insight Fora on Trade and Gender Equality and SMEs, with stakeholders from business associations, private sector, academics and civil society. The fora are used to share information on UK Government activity and seek stakeholder views to advise in specific trade matters. \nBIST and the Devolved Governments meet regularly at official level to facilitate information sharing in relation to gender equality and SME policy with regards to trade. \n\nThe Scottish Government has established a Gender Export Gap working group to deliver interventions which reduce barriers for women-led businesses to access exporting. The group meets quarterly and is comprised of organisations such as the Scottish Chambers of Commerce, enterprise agencies and Scottish Development International, as well as representation from Scottish Government trade policy and entrepreneurship policy officials. \n(https://www.gov.scot/groups/gender-export-gap-working-group/)"
     ]
