      "Women in Digital business (WIDB) was established by the International Labour Organization, International Training Centre of the International Labour Organization (ITCILO) and Microsoft Elevate to bridge the digital divide for women entrepreneurs in the developing world. WIDB works to provide women entrepreneurs with training and coaching opportunities to build their digital skills and leverage them to grow their business. We are currently seeking to evolve WIDB into a more integrated approach (as discussed above). \n\nhttps://www.widb.network/",
